# What must never be uploaded to Vercel.
#
# `excludeFiles` in vercel.json prunes the *function bundle*; this prunes the
# *upload*. Both are needed, and this one is the security-relevant half: a
# local `.env` is gitignored but very much present on disk, and the build's
# own filePathMap listed `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.preview` before this
# file existed (verified against `vercel build` output).

# Secrets. Never, under any circumstance (anti-goal #10).
.env
.env.*
*.env

# The test oracle and the corpus. The ground truth must not exist in the
# deployed artifact (anti-goal #1, reinforced at the packaging layer).
fixtures/
tests/

# Not needed at runtime, and large.
infra/
docs/
scripts/
.github/
Documents/
.venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.claude/
